<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms buys 23,300T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms buys 23,300T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two South Korean flour mills, Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd and Cheiljedang Corp, bought on Friday a combined total of 23,300 tonnes of U.S. wheat from a Japanese trading house, Marubeni Corp, traders said.  </p>
<p>Officials from the two companies confirmed the deals but declined to give further details.</p>
<p>Out of the total, Cheiljedang bought 11,300 tonnes at basis over December futures on the Chicago Board of Trade, traders said. Shipment was set for November 20-December 20 from the Pacific Northwest to the western port city of Inchun.</p>
<p>Details for the results are as follow:</p>
<p>Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/T (FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		5,500   $190.70</p>
<p>(protein max 10.8 percent)</p>
<p>  Soft White		1,500   $194.74</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5 percent)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 3,500   $196.58</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  1,500   $201.45</p>
<p>Cheiljedang Corp</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Bushel(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		3,000   $0.63</p>
<p>(protein max 10.8 percent)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  500   $0.74</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5 percent)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 3,800   $0.64</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  4,000   $0.93</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
